    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://n8n.flowroots.com/webhook/waterfall-contacts-batch",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json) }}",
        "options": {
          "batching": {
            "batch": {
              "batchSize": 3,
              "batchInterval": 500
            }
          },
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "fullResponse": true,
              "neverError": true
            }
          },
          "timeout": 1800000
        }
      },
      "id": "c4d50001-0018-4000-8000-000000000018",
      "name": "Fire Lanes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.4,
      "position": [
        3300,
        0
      ],
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "notes": "The three lanes. n8n runs a workflow's nodes one at a time, so parallel branches of Execute Workflow would still run batches one after another; the HTTP Request node is the one place n8n fires its items' requests together and awaits them all. Each item POSTs its batch to Waterfall Contacts Batch's door (POST /webhook/waterfall-contacts-batch, responds at its Respond Batch node after writing its own Hub row keyed <this execution>-<batchNum>). One answer per item, in order: 2xx with the counters, 5xx on a crash, an error item on a transport timeout (30 min). Never retried: a retry would run the paid tiers twice."
    },
